desc:RS90 [drum machine] (GFX)
//tags: instrument drum machine rhythm analogue 909 sequencer
//author: JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-drift, gfx-output, gfx-thick, gfx-ui, gfx-panel, gfx-dyn (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// RS90 - the RS series' house and techno machine, in the spirit of the mid-80s rhythm composer that mixed analogue
// drums with digital cymbals. No samples: the drums are synthesised live; the hats, crash and ride are synthesised
// when the plug-in loads ("baked") and played back through a low-bit stage, the way the original's cymbal chips did.
//
// VOICES (eleven channels)
//   BD  bass drum   a shaped sine with a fast pitch sweep: TUNE (the body's pitch +/-5 st, and the sweep's depth and
//                   length), ATTACK (the click), DECAY, LEVEL
//   SD  snare       two tuned oscillators and noise: TUNE, TONE (noise brightness), SNAPPY (noise level), LEVEL
//   LT, MT, HT      toms: a sine sweeping down, a breath of noise: TUNE, DECAY, LEVEL
//   RS  rim shot, CP  hand clap (four noise bursts and a tail): LEVEL
//   CH / OH  closed and open hats (baked): one LEVEL, CH DECAY, OH DECAY. CH cuts off a ringing OH.
//   CR  crash, RD  ride (baked): LEVEL, TUNE
//   ACCENT: how far apart accents and plain hits are (plain hits sit back, accents jump out; 50 % = about 6 dB).
//   The baked sounds are 6-bit (companded) at 32 kHz and pass through a gentle 11 kHz filter: the vintage grain.
//
// SEQUENCER: 16 patterns of 16 steps per channel (off / hit / accent), LAST STEP per pattern, SWING. It never starts
//   running by itself: press RUN. While REAPER plays, it locks to the timeline (bar 1 = step 1); while REAPER is
//   stopped, RUN free-runs at the project tempo. A new pattern takes over at the end of the bar.
// MIDI: notes play the voices too (GM drum map: 36 BD, 38 SD, 41 LT, 45 MT, 48 HT, 37 RS, 39 CP, 42 CH, 46 OH,
//   49 CR, 51 RD); velocity above 100 = accent. MIDI passes through.
//
// FOLLOW: the sequencer starts and stops with REAPER's transport (off by default: it never starts by itself).
// PATTERNS: a bank of 15 patterns; a new instance starts with them in patterns 1 - 15 (PATTERN > Load a pattern from
//   the bank brings any of them back). PATTERN also clears or copies the pattern.
// EDIT (layer B): a TUNE (+/- 12 semitones) and an amp envelope - ATTACK, DECAY, SUSTAIN, RELEASE - for every
//   instrument. SUSTAIN holds for the gate (one step from the sequencer, the held note from MIDI); SUSTAIN 100 % with
//   RELEASE at NATURAL (the default) leaves the sound as it is. Presets reset layer B to its defaults.
//
// SIGNAL FLOW: the voices > the FX strip, in this order: PHASER > DRIVE > COMP > DELAY (each with its IN key) >
//   THICK > LEVEL > the house output stage (CLIP, -0.3 dBFS). (THICK sits before the clipper so the ceiling holds.)
//   PHASER: six-stage, RATE, DEPTH, FEEDBACK, COLOUR (where it sweeps)      DRIVE: AMOUNT, TONE (level-matched)
//   COMP: THRESHOLD, RATIO, FAST / SLOW, MAKE-UP      DELAY: TIME (free) or note value (SYNC), FEEDBACK, DAMP, MIX
//
// DRIFT (0 - 100 %, 50 % = standard): ageing analogue parts.
//   tuning     each analogue drum wanders slowly (+/- 8 cents) and sits a little off (+/- 5 cents); the cymbal
//              chips' clock wanders a little too (+/- 3 cents)
//   ageing     each voice's decay sits a little off nominal (+/- 6 %)
//   supply     dense, accented playing sags the supply: the pitch dips (to -12 cents) and the level (to -0.4 dB),
//              recovering over about 300 ms
//   clock      the sequencer's steps jitter slightly (+/- 0.4 ms)
//   0 % = none, 100 % = twice the standard amount, a little faster.
//
// PAD ORDER AND COLOURS: the voices are laid out BD, SN, RIM, CLAP, HH, OH, HT, MT, LT, RD, CR (then the percussion)
//   on the panel, the grid and the EDIT page, colour-coded by family (kick brown, snare / rim red, clap orange,
//   hats yellow, toms green, cymbals blue, percussion violet; darker = lower). The MIDI notes are unchanged.
// GUI: in the dress of OB Q's OB face (dark panel, brown section bands, orange / yellow titles, cased LED keys).
//   The step grid: click a step to cycle off > hit > accent; drag to paint the same value along a row. Click a
//   track name to hear it. Values show while a knob is touched.
// PRESETS (12): kits - sounds, swing and FX, level-matched to Init on a groove; they never change the patterns.
//   (Patterns: see PATTERNS above.)
// Latency: 0 samples.
//
// TWEAK points are marked TWEAK.
// STATUS: Stable v2.0 (from the Lab, Oct 2026). v0.8 (wider ACCENT; complete: sound engine, sequencer, FX strip, faceplate, presets; BD TUNE now
//   also tunes the drum; delay DAMP now darkens every repeat; RUN / STOP brown).

import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-thick.jsfx-inc
import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-dyn.jsfx-inc

slider1:ac_lvl=50<0,100,1>-Accent (%)
slider2:bd_tune=50<0,100,1>-BD tune (%)
slider3:bd_att=50<0,100,1>-BD attack (%)
